  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance for Economic Crimes - Global Preventative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Preventative position develops and monitors the implementation of ECT technical assistance programs aimed at strengthening the preventative pillar of counterpart anti-money laundering and countering the financing of terrorism (AML/CFT) regimes. ECT programs under this pillar assist financial regulatory and supervisory authorities (particularly in the banking, securities, andinsurance sectors) to institute appropriate regulations; conduct effective AML/CFT compliance examinations; provide qualitative guidance to regulated entities; and, initiate civil and regulatory enforcement actions in instances of non-compliance. Assistance may also include work with non-financial sector reporting entities as defined by a jurisdictions AML/CFT legal framework, such as casinos, dealers in precious metals, real estate brokers and attorneys</narrative>
  </description>
